    <!-- Built-in advice (used when the Pi sends no steps, or after a correction) -->
    <string name="advice_paper_card">Remove tape and plastic parts and flatten boxes. Keep it clean and dry. Greasy or wet paper and card cannot be recycled.</string>
    <string name="advice_plastic">Empty, rinse and put the lid back on. Soft plastic film and bags often need a supermarket drop-off point.</string>
    <string name="advice_metal">Empty and rinse cans and tins. Scrunch clean foil into a ball. Empty aerosols are usually accepted.</string>
    <string name="advice_glass">Rinse bottles and jars and take the lids off. No drinking glasses, Pyrex or window glass.</string>
    <string name="advice_food_garden">Scrape food into your food caddy, lined with a compostable bag, never plastic. Garden waste goes in the garden bin or compost. No soil, stones or plastic pots.</string>
    <string name="advice_textile">Not for household recycling. Donate wearable items, or take worn-out fabric to a textile bank.</string>
    <string name="advice_special">Never put batteries or electricals in any bin. Take batteries to a shop or council collection point, and electricals to a retailer take-back or your recycling centre.</string>
    <string name="advice_general">This cannot be recycled at home. Bag it and put it in your general waste bin.</string>

